            "width": 37.98882681564246,
            "height": 8.830022075055187,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:1.5em;\"><strong>INFORMATION TEXT (Part 2)</strong></span></p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "55aaf4d3-f7e3-4a3e-9196-01a6f7474f94"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Evolution and Experimentation</strong><br>\nThroughout his career, Matisse continually experimented with different media and techniques, including sculpture and printmaking. His travels to places like Morocco influenced his palette and subject matter, introducing new themes and spatial complexities into his work.</p>\n\n<p><strong>\"Dance\" and \"Music\"</strong><br>\nCommissioned by the Russian businessman Sergei Shchukin, Matisse's iconic murals \"Dance\" and \"Music\" are seminal works that reflect his ongoing interest in depicting the human form in motion, using color and composition to convey emotional intensity.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Chapelle du Rosaire</strong><br>\nIn his later years, Matisse devoted much of his energy to designing the Chapelle du Rosaire in Vence, France. This project allowed him to synthesize his artistic vision in architecture, stained glass, and murals, and is considered one of his greatest achievements.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
