            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Cut-Outs</strong><br>\nWhen ill health prevented him from painting, Matisse began creating cut-outs, which involved cutting into painted paper to create lively and intricate compositions. These works represented a breakthrough in terms of their simplicity and directness.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Personal Life</strong><br>\nMatisse was known for his intense work ethic and his belief in the importance of an artist's environment for creative work. He created a vibrant living space filled with objects that inspired his art and was known for his charismatic teaching style.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Death and Legacy</strong><br>\nMatisse died in 1954, leaving behind a vast oeuvre that continued to influence the art world. His bold use of color and pioneering spirit contributed to major developments in modern art, and his works remain celebrated for their beauty and innovation.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
